<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakata</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sakata is a port city at the mouth of the Mogami River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamagata-prefecture">Yamagata Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a> it shipped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> of the Shōnai plain and the Mogami valley to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> and Edo on the western sea route, and merchant families such as the Homma made fortunes there. It lay within the Shōnai Domain.</p></div>
